# Every tracked text file is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# The repository normalizes to LF (0.0.16) and CI runs `prettier --check`, whose
# default endOfLine is LF. On Windows, Git for Windows defaults to
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so every checkout rewrote the working tree to CRLF and
# `npm run ci` failed `format:check` on ~153 files whose committed content was
# already correct. `eol=lf` makes the working tree LF too, so the local gate agrees
# with CI instead of failing on line endings alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets keep whatever bytes they were committed with.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
